@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Lists and tables)

Bulleted, numbered and definition lists, tables, interlinear glosses and paragraph settings.

@section(Lists)

@subsection(@@ul)

A bulleted list — one item per line, or item per entry.

@ul
First
Second
@end

@ul(cols=3, mono, plain) … @end

@ul(cols=2, order=row, sort=az, marker=check)
wires
battery
lamp
switch
@end

@ul(marker=disc)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=circle)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=square)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=dash)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=arrow)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=chevron)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=triangle)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=star)
one
two
@end

@ul(marker=none)
one
two
@end

@ul(order=col, sort=za)
x
y
@end

@ul(sort=len)
abc
a
ab
@end

@ul(sort=natural)
v10
v9
@end

@@itemize is the same as @@ul:
@itemize
@item First
@end

@subsection(@@ol)

A numbered list.

@ol
First
Second
@end

@ol(I)
Roman one
Roman two
@end

@ol(1.1)
Top
@ol
Nested
@end
@end

@ol(cols=2)
one
two
three
four
@end

@ol(order=row, sort=az, mono, style=a, cols=2)
pear
apple
fig
cherry
@end

@ol(cols=2, order=col, sort=za)
b
a
c
d
@end

@ol(sort=len)
long word here
short
mid size
@end

@ol(sort=natural)
item 10
item 2
item 1
@end

@@enum and @@enumerate are the same as @@ol:
@enum
@item First
@end
@enumerate
@item First
@end

@subsection(@@item)

One list entry, LaTeX-style.

@subsection(@@list)

A COLUMN list: one comma-separated run — across as many lines as you like — laid out in N columns, balanced so no two columns differ by more than one item.

@list(cols=5)
a, b, c,
d, e
@end

@list(cols=auto, mono)
R1, R2, C1, L1
@end

@list(cols=4, order=row)
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8
@end

@list(cols=4, sort=az)
pear, apple, fig, plum
@end

@list(cols=3, marker=arrow)
in, through, out
@end

@list(ol, cols=2)
first, second, third, fourth
@end

@list(cols=4, sep=;)
Ohm, volt; amp, watt; farad; henry
@end

@list(plain, cols=3)
red, green, blue
@end

@list(ol, style=A, cols=2)
first, second, third, fourth
@end

@list(cols=3, order=col, sort=za)
b, a, c, d, e, f
@end

@list(sort=len)
abc, a, ab
@end

@list(sort=natural)
v10, v9, v1
@end

@list(marker=disc)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=circle)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=square)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=dash)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=chevron)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=triangle)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=check)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=star)
one, two
@end

@list(marker=none)
one, two
@end

@subsection(@@dl)

A description list: one term: definition per line — the term bold, the definition after it, a hanging indent, the same on paper.

@dl
Resistor: a part that opposes current
Capacitor: a part that stores charge
@end

@section(Tables)

@subsection(@@table)

A table — rows on newlines, cells on commas (sep= changes that).

@table
@row
@cell
@graph(type=bar, src=a.csv)
@endcell
@cell
@graph(type=pie, src=b.csv)
@endcell
@endtable

@table
@row
@cell A
@cell B
@endtable

@table
Head1, Head2
a, b
@endtable

@table(style=grid, align=l,r,r)
Part, Ohms, Watts
R1, 100, 0.25
@endtable

@table(widths=30% 70%)
Term, Definition
@endtable

@table(sep=|)
Name | Value, with a comma
A | 1, 2
@endtable

@table
@row
@cell
@graph(type=bar, src=a.csv)
@endcell
@cell
@graph(type=pie, src=b.csv)
@endcell
@endtable

@table(header=1, zebra, compact, accent=#1d4ed8, caption=Readings with stripes, width=80%, label=tab-read, footer=1)
Part, Volts, Amps
R1, 2.0, 0.1
R2, 4.0, 0.1
Total, 6.0, 0.1
@endtable

@table(roomy, rows=2, bg=#fef9c3, columns=3, color=#b91c1c)
A, B, C
1, 2, 3
4, 5, 6
@endtable

@table(cells=r2..3 c2..3, bg=#dcfce7)
A, B, C
1, 2, 3
4, 5, 6
@endtable

@table(paint=r1..2:yellow; c(1 3):red text)
A, B, C
1, 2, 3
@endtable

@table(scramble)
Step, Action
1, Read the meter
2, Write it down
3, Switch off
@endtable

@table(side)
X, Y
1, 2
@endtable

@table(rotate=90)
A wide, table, turned, sideways
1, 2, 3, 4
@endtable

In a two-column paper, span crosses both columns: @table(span)
Key, Value
a, 1
@endtable

@table(border)
A, B
1, 2
@endtable

@subsection(@@row)

Starts a table row in the explicit form, where newlines mean nothing and only row and cell divide the table.

@subsection(@@endcell)

Closes a cell.

@subsection(@@endrow)

Closes a row.

@section(Paragraphs and glosses)

@subsection(@@par)

A passage with its own paragraph settings, up to end: first-line indent, hanging indent, spacing between paragraphs, line spacing, alignment, kept on one page, no hyphenation.

@par(indent=1.5em, spacing=0.4em)
…paragraphs…
@end

@par(hang=2em)
…a reference list…
@end

@par(leading=2, align=justify, keep)
…
@end

@par(nohyphen)
A passage that never hyphenates a word at the end of a line, however long the words: electroencephalography, interdisciplinary.
@end

@subsection(@@interlinear)

A glossed example, numbered (1), (2)… First line the example, word by word (in italic); each line after it glosses those words, one gloss per word, so they line up in columns.

@interlinear(label=dog)
Der Hund bell-t
the dog bark-3SG
'The dog is barking.'
@end
